  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\[ \\begin{aligned} N&=\\frac{\\sqrt{\\sqrt5+2}+\\sqrt{\\sqrt5-2}} {\\sqrt{\\sqrt5+1}}\\\\ &\\quad-\\sqrt{3-2\\sqrt2}, \\end{aligned} \\] then \\(N\\) equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\sqrt2-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{\\frac52}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "1"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1976-p27.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(T\\) be the first fraction. Its numerator squared is \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(\\sqrt5+2)+(\\sqrt5-2)\\\\ &\\quad+2\\sqrt{(\\sqrt5+2)(\\sqrt5-2)}\\\\ &=2\\sqrt5+2. \\end{aligned} \\] Thus \\(T^2=\\frac{2\\sqrt5+2}{\\sqrt5+1}=2,\\) and \\(T=\\sqrt2.\\) Also \\(\\sqrt{3-2\\sqrt2}=\\sqrt2-1.\\) Hence \\(N=\\sqrt2-(\\sqrt2-1)=1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Square the numerator of the large fraction before simplifying it",
        "Recognize \\(3-2\\sqrt2\\) as \\((\\sqrt2-1)^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
